       header says so. The EMITTING paths exist in the GTK-free core
       (pn_knob_scroll, pn_switch_toggle, pn_inject_fire,
       pn_keypad_press_code) but their only callers are the GTK event
       handlers in lib/pn-worksheet.c (the knob's at the scroll handler,
       ~5287). The Worksheet interface (#40) was designed around
       authoring; "operate a control" was never part of it. The
       Engine interface grew ActivateWidget (src/pn-application.c)
       for the panel/desktop viewers, Switch and Inject only.
       DBUS-API.md's own worked example works around the gap: it adds
       a Knob and then injects into the Topic node beside it.
